# m4_decoupling  2026-10-29 17:50:06
A-part = |A1|^2 |A2|^2 / (X1 X2),  S-part = prod_i |S_i|^2 / D_i,  rho_cross = E[A-part S-part] / (E[A-part] E[S-part])   (weighted over kept rows).
rho_cross ~ 1: the plain and slot polynomials are uncorrelated, so E/K = (plain factor) x (slot factor), each O(1) and not growing.
(A1, A2 are two views of the same L-function: E[A-part] ~ 2 E|A1|^2 E|A2|^2 ;  slots with equal w_i are the same polynomial: E[S-part] = k! (E|S|^2)^k - both are inside the factors, not in rho_cross.)
